### PS-CACHE-HOST:2025 — Web Cache Poisoning, Web Cache Deception & HTTP Host Header Attack Defense

- **Official Reference:** [PS-CACHE-HOST:2025 Web Cache Poisoning, Web Cache Deception & HTTP Host Header Attack Defense](https://portswigger.net/web-security/web-cache-poisoning)

- **Mapped CWEs:** `CWE-444, CWE-644 (Improper Neutralization of HTTP Headers for Scripting Syntax)`

- **Risk Summary:** Web Cache Poisoning injects payloads via unkeyed headers (`X-Forwarded-Host`, `X-Original-URL`), Web Cache Deception tricks CDNs into caching private `/account/profile/nonexistent.css` responses, and Host Header attacks poison password-reset links.

- **Primary Defensive Control:** Never build password-reset or asset URLs from `Host` or `X-Forwarded-Host`; pin a canonical `PUBLIC_BASE_URL`, validate `Host` against a strict allow-list, and set `Cache-Control: private, no-store` on all authenticated routes.

